    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Thomson Reuters is a public company, traded as TRI, founded in 2008 and headquartered in Toronto. Its site describes it as delivering \"technology with purpose\" for professionals, and it reports a CIK of 0001075124. The company's own material frames its AI work around legal, tax, accounting, risk, fraud, and government sectors, with products including CoCounsel, Westlaw AI, Practical Law, and ONESOURCE+, which it describes as bringing tax, trade, legal, and risk together in an AI-powered connected approach.\n\nIts tracked AI product is CoCounsel, which the company acquired with Casetext. The site describes CoCounsel as agentic AI for legal professionals, grounded in Westlaw and Practical Law content, and says it is built on principles the company calls \"Fiduciary-Grade AI.\" Thomson Reuters says it is launching its first production-grade workflows on CoCounsel for multi-step work, and that global law firm Greenberg Traurig deployed the next generation of CoCounsel Legal in August 2026. The site also cites Justly Prudent using CoCounsel and Westlaw AI to increase litigation capacity by 100%. CoCounsel is tracked as legal research and litigation support software with Westlaw integration, and attorney work product risk is noted alongside it.\n\nThe site also points to two company reports, the Future of Professionals Report 2026 and the 2026 AI in Professional Services Report, the latter drawing on perspectives from more than 1,500 professionals. Both describe AI as now embedded in professional work, with value depending on execution, strategy, and infrastructure, and with risks surfacing across clients, talent, and governance.",
